# 🚨 CURSOR RULES - Max Baby Shopify Theme

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: READ THIS BEFORE ANY CODE CHANGES

This is a Shopify Liquid theme project for a Hebrew (RTL) baby products store. ALL code must follow these rules.

---

## 🔴 RULE #1: LIQUID ONLY - NO EXCEPTIONS

**MANDATORY:** ALL code must be written in **Shopify Liquid** only.

✅ **ALLOWED:**
- `.liquid` files (sections, blocks, snippets, templates, layouts)
- CSS inside `{% stylesheet %}` or `{% style %}` tags
- JavaScript inside `{% javascript %}` tags
- Liquid syntax: `{{ }}` for output, `{% %}` for logic

❌ **FORBIDDEN:**
- React, Vue, Angular, or any JavaScript frameworks
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, or any CSS frameworks requiring build tools
- Build tools (Webpack, Vite, Rollup, etc.)
- npm packages or Node.js modules
- Any code that requires compilation

**Why?** Shopify themes only understand Liquid. Any other code will break.

---

## 🔴 RULE #2: ALWAYS USE design.json FOR STYLING

**MANDATORY:** Before writing any CSS, check `design.json` for:
- Colors (use exact hex codes from `design.json.colors`)
- Typography (fonts, sizes, weights from `design.json.typography`)
- Spacing (use `design.json.spacing` values)
- Borders (radius, width from `design.json.borders`)
- Shadows (from `design.json.shadows`)
- Transitions (from `design.json.transitions`)
- Breakpoints (from `design.json.breakpoints`)

**Example:**
```liquid
{% stylesheet %}
  .button {
    background: #CDB9A2; /* from design.json.colors.primary */
    padding: 12px 24px; /* from design.json.components.button.primary.padding */
    border-radius: 8px; /* from design.json.borders.radius.md */
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

**If design.json doesn't have a value you need:**
1. First, update `design.json` with the new value
2. Then use it in your code
3. **Never hardcode values without updating design.json first**

### How to Reference design.json Values

**In CSS:**
```liquid
{% stylesheet %}
  .button {
    /* Read values directly from design.json */
    background: #CDB9A2; /* design.json.colors.primary */
    padding: 12px 24px; /* design.json.components.button.primary.padding */
    border-radius: 8px; /* design.json.borders.radius.md */
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

**If design.json doesn't have a value you need:**
1. First update design.json with the new value
2. Then use it in your code
3. **Never hardcode without updating design.json first**

---

## 🔴 RULE #3: RTL (RIGHT-TO-LEFT) SUPPORT IS MANDATORY

**MANDATORY:** All sections, blocks, and snippets must support Hebrew RTL.

**Required CSS:**
```liquid
{% stylesheet %}
  .section {
    direction: rtl;
    text-align: right;
  }
  
  /* Use logical properties for spacing */
  .element {
    padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-md); /* instead of padding-left */
    margin-inline-end: var(--spacing-sm); /* instead of margin-right */
  }
  
  /* Flexbox RTL support */
  .flex-container {
    flex-direction: row-reverse; /* if needed */
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

**Liquid RTL considerations:**
- Use `{{ 'key' | t }}` for all text (translations in `locales/he.json`)
- Never hardcode Hebrew text directly in Liquid files
- Test all layouts in RTL mode

### Hebrew Typography Requirements (MANDATORY)

**Fonts:**
- Headings: `font-family: 'Heebo', sans-serif;`
- Body text: `font-family: 'Assistant', sans-serif;`
- **NEVER use fonts that don't support Hebrew characters**

**Load Google Fonts in layout/theme.liquid:**
```liquid
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Heebo:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Assistant:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

---

## 🔴 RULE #4: SHOPIFY THEME ARCHITECTURE

**Directory Structure:**
- `sections/` - Full-width page components (`.liquid` files)
- `blocks/` - Reusable, nestable components (`.liquid` files)
- `snippets/` - Reusable code fragments (`.liquid` files)
- `templates/` - Page structure definitions (`.json` files)
- `layout/` - Top-level HTML wrappers (`.liquid` files)
- `assets/` - Static files (CSS, JS, images)
- `config/` - Theme settings
- `locales/` - Translation files

**File Requirements:**

**Sections:**
- Must be `.liquid` files in `sections/`
- Must include `{% schema %}` block
- Use `section.id` for unique CSS classes
- Example: `sections/hero.liquid`

**Blocks:**
- Must be `.liquid` files in `blocks/`
- Must include `{% doc %}` tag at the top
- Must include `{% schema %}` block
- Must include `{{ block.shopify_attributes }}` in HTML
- Example: `blocks/text.liquid`

**Snippets:**
- Must be `.liquid` files in `snippets/`
- Must include `{% doc %}` tag at the top with `@param` documentation
- Accept parameters via `{% render 'snippet', param: value %}`
- Example: `snippets/image.liquid`

### When to Use Sections vs Blocks vs Snippets

**Sections (sections/):**
- Full-width page components
- Editable via theme editor
- Can contain blocks
- Examples: Hero, Product Grid, Testimonials
- Use when: Merchants need to customize via UI

**Blocks (blocks/):**
- Nestable, repeatable components within sections
- Editable via theme editor
- Examples: Testimonial Card, Feature Item, USP Badge
- Must include `{{ block.shopify_attributes }}`
- Use when: Merchants need to add/remove repeated items

**Snippets (snippets/):**
- Pure code reuse (no theme editor interaction)
- Rendered programmatically via `{% render %}`
- Examples: Product Card, Icon, Button
- Accept parameters only
- Use when: Code reuse without merchant customization

**Rule of thumb:**
- Need theme editor control → Section or Block
- Pure code reuse → Snippet

---

## 🔴 RULE #5: SCHEMA REQUIREMENTS

**Every Section and Block MUST include a `{% schema %}` block:**

```liquid
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.section_name",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "t:labels.title",
      "default": "Default Title"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:general.section_name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
```

**Schema Best Practices:**
- Use translation keys (`t:general.key`) for all labels
- For single CSS property settings → use CSS variables
- For multiple CSS properties → use CSS classes
- Validate schema JSON using `schemas/section.json` or `schemas/theme_block.json`

**Section generation requirements (Cursor AI):**
- For **every new Shopify section** generated by Cursor:
  - ALWAYS include a complete `{% schema %}` block with all required `settings` (and `blocks` if relevant).
  - ALWAYS include a `"presets"` entry so the section is visible and addable in the Theme Editor.
  - ALWAYS infer and define all necessary input `type`s (for example: `text`, `richtext`, `image_picker`, `range`, `checkbox`, `select`, `url`, `product_list`, `collection_list`, etc.) based on the described functionality of the section.
  - NEVER omit schema just because the section is “simple” – every section must be fully editable via the Theme Editor.
  - Prefer clear, self-documenting `id` names in snake_case that match the semantics of the setting (for example: `hero_title`, `background_image`, `cta_label`).

---

## 🔴 RULE #6: TRANSLATION REQUIREMENTS

**MANDATORY:** All user-facing text must use translation filters.

✅ **CORRECT:**
```liquid
<h2>{{ 'sections.hero.title' | t }}</h2>
<button>{{ 'products.add_to_cart' | t }}</button>
```

❌ **WRONG:**
```liquid
<h2>כותרת</h2>
<button>הוסף לעגלה</button>
```

**Translation File:**
- Update `locales/en.default.json` with all new keys
- Use hierarchical keys: `sections.hero.title`
- Maximum 3 levels deep
- Use snake_case for key names

---

## 🔴 RULE #7: PROJECT CONTEXT AWARENESS

**This is a baby products store with:**
- ~100 products (beds, changing tables, toys, room sets)
- Hebrew (RTL) interface
- Israeli market (ILS currency)
- Mobile-first (70%+ traffic expected on mobile)
- Fast timeline (5-7 days to launch)

**Key Templates:**
- `templates/product.json` - Serves ALL 100 products automatically
- `templates/collection.json` - Serves all collection pages
- `templates/index.json` - Homepage
- `templates/cart.json` - Shopping cart

**Product Organization (CRITICAL FOR FILTERS):**
- Every product MUST have consistent `Product Type`:
  - "מיטות תינוק" (cribs)
  - "שידות החתלה" (changing tables)  
  - "צעצועים" (toys)
  - "חדרי תינוקות" (nursery sets)
- Every product MUST have `Vendor` (brand name: סגל, טל, etc.)
- These fields enable automated collections and native Shopify filtering
- **Be consistent!** "מיטת תינוק" ≠ "מיטות תינוק" will break filters

**Key Principle:** Build once, use everywhere. Never hardcode product-specific data.

---

## 🔴 RULE #8: MOBILE-FIRST RESPONSIVE DESIGN

**MANDATORY:** All sections must be mobile-first and responsive.

**Use design.json breakpoints:**
```liquid
{% stylesheet %}
  .section {
    /* Mobile styles (default) */
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  
  @media (min-width: 768px) { /* design.json.breakpoints.mobile */
    .section {
      padding: var(--spacing-xl);
    }
  }
  
  @media (min-width: 1024px) { /* design.json.breakpoints.tablet */
    .section {
      padding: var(--spacing-2xl);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
```

**Test on mobile first!** Most Israeli customers shop on mobile.

---

## 🔴 RULE #9: PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

**MANDATORY:**
- Page load time < 3 seconds
- Use `{% stylesheet %}` and `{% javascript %}` tags (not external files)
- Optimize images with `image_url` filter
- Use `{% preload_tag %}` for critical assets
- Minimize Liquid loops (max 50 iterations per `for` loop)

**Image Optimization:**
```liquid
{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag }}
```

---

## 🔴 RULE #10: SHOPIFY FILTERS AND OBJECTS

**Use Shopify Liquid objects and filters correctly:**

**Common Objects:**
- `product` - Product data
- `collection` - Collection data
- `cart` - Shopping cart
- `shop` - Shop information
- `customer` - Customer data

**Common Filters:**
- `{{ price | money }}` - Format money
- `{{ image | image_url: width: 800 }}` - Image URL
- `{{ 'key' | t }}` - Translation
- `{{ text | escape }}` - Escape HTML

**Never hardcode product data!** Always use Liquid objects.

---

## 🔴 RULE #11: CODE QUALITY

**Before submitting code, verify:**
1. ✅ All code is Liquid (no React/Vue/TypeScript)
2. ✅ All styling uses `design.json` values
3. ✅ RTL support is implemented
4. ✅ All text uses translation filters
5. ✅ `{% schema %}` block is included (sections/blocks)
6. ✅ `{% doc %}` tag is included (snippets/blocks)
7. ✅ Mobile-responsive
8. ✅ Uses `section.id` or `block.id` for unique CSS classes
9. ✅ No hardcoded product-specific data
10. ✅ Follows Shopify Liquid best practices

---

## 🔴 RULE #12: WORKFLOW PROCESS

**Design Validation Process (BEFORE building sections):**
1. Create design.json from design inspiration screenshots
2. Build sections/component-showcase.liquid to validate all design.json values
3. Test showcase in theme editor - does everything look correct?
4. **If not → fix design.json, NOT the code!**
5. Only after showcase is perfect → start building real sections

**When creating new sections/blocks/snippets:**

1. **Check design.json first** - Does it have the values you need?
2. **Create the file** - Use correct directory (`sections/`, `blocks/`, `snippets/`)
3. **Add documentation** - `{% doc %}` tag with `@param` for snippets/blocks
4. **Add styling** - Use `{% stylesheet %}` with `design.json` values
5. **Add schema** - `{% schema %}` block for sections/blocks
6. **Test RTL** - Verify Hebrew text and layout
7. **Test mobile** - Verify responsive design
8. **Add translations** - Update `locales/en.default.json`

---

## 🔴 RULE #13: NEVER DO THESE THINGS

❌ **NEVER:**
- Write React, Vue, or any framework code
- Hardcode colors, spacing, or typography (use `design.json`)
- Hardcode Hebrew text (use translation filters)
- Create product-specific templates (use `product.json` for all products)
- Skip RTL support
- Skip mobile responsiveness
- Skip `{% schema %}` blocks
- Use external CSS/JS files (use `{% stylesheet %}` and `{% javascript %}`)
- Create duplicate code (use snippets for reusable parts)
- Hardcode product data (use Liquid objects)

---

## 🔴 RULE #14: IMAGE OPTIMIZATION

**MANDATORY for all images:**

```liquid
{%- comment -%} Product images {%- endcomment -%}
{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: product.title }}

{%- comment -%} Collection banners {%- endcomment -%}
{{ collection.image | image_url: width: 1920 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy' }}

{%- comment -%} Section background images {%- endcomment -%}
{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1920 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy' }}
```

**Image Size Guidelines:**
- Product grid thumbnails: 400-600px
- Product page main image: 800-1200px  
- Hero/banner images: 1920px
- Small thumbnails: 100-200px

**Always use:**
- `loading: 'lazy'` attribute (except above-the-fold hero images)
- Shopify `image_url` filter with explicit width
- Descriptive `alt` text for accessibility

