## 🔴 RULE #15: CORE PRINCIPLE – NEVER EDIT DAWN'S ORIGINAL SECTIONS

**NEVER edit core Dawn theme files directly. Always extend via new custom sections instead.**

- Editing core Dawn files (for example: `main-product.liquid`, `featured-collection.liquid`, `theme.liquid`, `header.liquid`, `footer.liquid`) can cause **loss of customizations** when the theme is updated or reinstalled.
- **Always create NEW section files** in the `sections/` directory instead of modifying Dawn’s original sections.
- **Naming convention for all custom sections:**
  - `custom-[feature-name].liquid`
  - Examples:
    - `custom-hero.liquid`
    - `custom-testimonials.liquid`
    - `custom-product-usp.liquid`
- For **minor tweaks only** (small text blocks, extra HTML, one-off content):
  - Prefer using Dawn’s built‑in **“Custom Liquid”** blocks **inside the Theme Editor** instead of creating or editing files.
- When a change *seems* to require editing a core file:
  - First, try:
    - A new `custom-*.liquid` section that you add to the relevant template
    - Or a “Custom Liquid” block in an existing section
  - Only if absolutely impossible, and **with explicit warning**, consider touching core Dawn code.

---

## 🔴 RULE #16: SECTION CREATION STANDARDS

**Every new custom section MUST be fully configurable and visible in the Theme Editor.**

- **Schema block (MANDATORY):**
  - Every new section MUST include a **complete** `{% schema %}` block.
  - Schema MUST define:
    - `"name"` – human‑readable name (use translations where possible)
    - `"settings"` – all configurable options for the section
    - `"blocks"` – for repeatable/dynamic content (for example: list of testimonials, feature items, icons, etc.) where relevant
    - `"presets"` – so the section appears in the “Add section” list in the Theme Editor.
- **Presets (MANDATORY):**
  - Every section MUST define at least one preset:
    ```json
    "presets": [
      {
        "name": "Custom [Feature Name]",
        "category": "Custom"
      }
    ]
    ```
  - This ensures the section is visible and addable from the Theme Editor UI.

- **Input types (MANDATORY):**
  - Choose input `type` according to the actual functionality of the section:
    - `text` – קצר, שורה אחת
    - `textarea` / `richtext` – טקסט ארוך/מעוצב
    - `image_picker` – בחירת תמונה
    - `url` – קישור
    - `color` – בחירת צבע (אם לא מנוהל דרך `design.json`)
    - `range` – ערך נומרי עם טווח (spacing, number of columns, opacity)
    - `select` – בחירה מתוך רשימה סגורה (layout, alignment, style)
    - `checkbox` – דגל on/off (להציג/להסתיר אלמנט)
  - לכל שדה:
    - `id` ברור ב־snake_case (לדוגמה: `hero_heading`, `cta_label`, `background_image`)
    - `label` עם מפתח תרגום (`t:`) כשאפשר
    - `default` הגיוני שמייצר תצוגה טובה כברירת מחדל.

- **Blocks for repeatable content:**
  - עבור תוכן שחוזר על עצמו (כרטיסי פיצ'ר, המלצות, אייקונים, שורות טקסט):
    - הוסף `"blocks"` ל־schema.
    - השתמש ב־`block.settings.*` בתוך ה־HTML.
    - אל תשכפל div‑ים ידנית בקוד – תן למשתמש להוסיף/להוריד בלוקים בעריכה.

- **Semantic HTML:**
  - השתמש בשדות `"tag"` ו־`"class"` ב־schema כאשר מתאים:
    - `"tag": "section"`
    - `"class": "custom-section custom-[feature-name]"`
  - ב־HTML:
    - הוסף classes עם `section.id` כדי להבטיח scope ייחודי:
      ```liquid
      <section class="custom-[feature-name] section-{{ section.id }}">
      ```

---

## 🔴 RULE #17: FILE ORGANIZATION FOR CUSTOM SECTIONS

- **Naming convention:**
  - All custom sections MUST be created in `sections/` and their filenames MUST start with `custom-`.
  - Examples:
    - `sections/custom-hero.liquid`
    - `sections/custom-featured-products.liquid`
    - `sections/custom-product-usp-bar.liquid`

- **Modular & reusable:**
  - Design every custom section so it can be reused on multiple templates (homepage, collections, product page, etc.).
  - Avoid product/collection‑specific logic – use Liquid objects (`product`, `collection`, `settings`) and schema settings.

- **Documentation:**
  - At the top of each custom section, add a clear Liquid comment describing:
    - What the section does
    - Where it is intended to be used
    - Any important settings/blocks
  - Example:
    ```liquid
    {%- comment -%}
      custom-hero.liquid
      Reusable hero section with background image, heading, subheading, and CTA button.
      Intended for homepage and landing pages.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    ```

---

## 🔴 RULE #18: SAFETY RULES & WORKFLOW

- **NEVER work on the live theme directly:**
  - Always duplicate the live theme in Shopify Admin:
    - `Online Store → Themes → Actions → Duplicate`
  - Work only on the duplicated theme (development/staging), not on the currently published theme.

- **Git & version control (recommended):**
  - Use Git to track changes in the theme files:
    - Commit frequently with clear messages.
    - Use branches for new features/experiments.
    - Keep `main`/`master` stable and deployable.
  - When using `shopify theme pull` / `shopify theme push`, ensure your local repo is in sync.

- **Core Dawn safety warnings:**
  - Before **any** modification to files shipped with Dawn (for example `header.liquid`, `footer.liquid`, `product.liquid`, `collection.liquid`, `theme.liquid`):
    - Prefer:
      - New `custom-*` sections
      - “Custom Liquid” blocks
    - If still necessary:
      - Add a **clear warning comment** in the file explaining why a core file was edited.
      - Make sure the change is tracked in Git with a clear commit message.
  - Cursor AI should **always**:
    - Suggest a **custom section** solution first.
    - Warn explicitly when a requested change would touch a core Dawn file.

---

## 🔴 RULE #19: EXAMPLE CUSTOM SECTION TEMPLATE (STANDARD)

Use this as the baseline structure for all new custom sections:

```liquid
{%- comment -%}
  sections/custom-[feature-name].liquid
  Short description of what this section does and where it's used.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="custom-[feature-name] section-{{ section.id }} page-width">
  <!-- Custom section content goes here -->
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Custom [Feature Name]",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "custom-section custom-[feature-name]",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Default heading"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [

  ],
